.TH MUNMAP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
munmap \- unmap a memory range
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B int munmap(void* address, size_t byte_count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unmaps the Linux memory range beginning at a page\-aligned address.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmap (3crunch),
.BR munmap (2)
